  "rationale": "The target after “Ben and the” is a noun, but apples and pears receive almost no probability; the same batch also shows “The” followed by needles. Existing strong noun rules do not consistently cover the ordinary determiner-to-noun pattern. Add a moderate suffix rule to common noun roots so that a final determiner supports those nouns without asserting a particular noun or making other continuations impossible. This may add noun probability in contexts where an adjective would be the next word, so the rule is deliberately not overwhelming. The malformed free generation is diagnostic rather than supervision and does not justify copying its sequence into a grammar.",
